course: dictionary
lesson: 8772
title: Shabby: old, worn and a bit mean
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Shabby is a word you will meet often in stories. It describes something that has been used so much that it looks old, worn and untidy. «The passage is long, gloomy, and, to tell the truth, decidedly shabby» means the passage is not broken, just old and worn out.
explain: Shabby can also describe clothes or people. A shabby coat has worn patches and faded colour. The words around shabby give you the clues: a passage, a door-mat or a house tells you about old things, while clothes tell you about how someone looks.
explain: Shabby can also mean unfair or mean. «That was a shabby way to treat her» is about how someone behaved, not about old things. Read the whole sentence before you decide which meaning fits, and check by swapping in your meaning.
fact: Shabby means old, worn and untidy from a lot of use.
fact: «Shabby» can describe a place or thing, like «a shabby passage» or «a shabby door-mat».
fact: «Shabby» can describe clothes that are old and worn.
fact: «Shabby» can also mean unfair or mean, as in «a shabby trick».
fact: Informal talk uses «not shabby» to mean quite good.
exercise: «The Rat digs on and finds a shabby door-mat.» What does shabby mean here? | Brand new and bright | *Old, worn and untidy | Wet and muddy from the rain | Very large and heavy
exercise: «The passage is long, gloomy, and, to tell the truth, decidedly shabby.» What does shabby tell you about the passage? | *It is old and worn out | It is shiny and new | It is full of light | It is very narrow and steep
exercise: Ella says, «That was a shabby way to treat her.» What is shabby telling us? | *That the treatment was unfair or mean | That the person was wearing worn-out clothes | That the treatment was very old | That the treatment was quite good
test: In «a shabby little home», what does shabby mean? | Very tall | Loud and cheerful | *Old and worn | Painted bright blue
test: Nadia says about her drawing, «Not too shabby.» What does she mean? | Very old and worn | *Quite good | Unfair to everyone | Dirty and wet from the rain
exam: The Mole goes into «a cold, small, shabby, long-forgotten house»: what does shabby tell you about the house? | Full of gold and jewels | *Dusty and worn, and not cared for | Brand new and shiny | Very large and grand
